WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:01.607
- So Hensler declares that,

00:00:01.607 --> 00:00:04.070
"The marriage has become
very unsupportable,

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:07.700
unless she consents to having
her mouth surgically closed."

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:09.240
My God, man.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:12.420
Holy cow, you put this
in front of the court.

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:14.740
A pleading is a document
that you file with the court.

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:17.880
And whenever I file a pleading,
it is well-researched,

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.370
it makes good faith,
well-reasoned arguments,

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:23.070
and it is spell checked
within an inch of its life.

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:25.070
But the pleadings we're
talking about today

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:27.270
have none of those things.

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:30.520
These are the most bizarre
and ridiculous pleadings

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:33.170
that have ever been filed
in an American court.

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:38.170
We start with the Iowa man
who requested trial by combat.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:41.130
So in America, we take
pride in a judicial system

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:43.260
that allows anyone to have
their grievances heard

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:45.570
before a neutral judge
or a jury of their peers.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:48.410
And instead of resolving
disagreements through duals,

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:50.070
like "The Days of Yore,"

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:53.300
legal disputes can be addressed
in a calm and civil manner.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:56.790
Well, that is the ideal, at least.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:01:00.280
Because reality is often
much, much different.

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:03.430
Enter David Ostrom of Paola, Kansas,

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:06.050
who during a heated custody
battle against his ex-wife,

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:08.570
requested an Iowa court
turn their legal battle

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:10.210
into a literal battle,

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:12.150
complete with samurai swords.

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:13.760
In an effort to resolve a dispute

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:16.400
over his ability to communicate
with his two children

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.870
and get his ex-wife to pay property taxes

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:20.220
on their former home,

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:22.230
Mr. Ostrom filed a motion challenging

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:23.970
his former spouse and her attorney

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:26.850
to quote "trial by combat."

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:30.130
Mr. Ostrom was purportedly
inspired by Richard Luthmann,

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:33.070
a Staten Island attorney and
"Game of Thrones" officinato,

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:34.730
who requested a trial by combat

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:37.660
to settle a dispute with
another lawyer and his clients.

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:39.797
In Mr. Ostrom's motion he wrote,

00:01:39.797 --> 00:01:41.480
"My ex-wife and her attorney indicated

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:43.000
they have destroyed me legally,

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:44.620
now I wish to give them the chance

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:46.570
to meet me on the field of battle,

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:50.180
where I will rend their
souls from their bodies."

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:52.510
Mr. Ostrom, ever the chivalrous type,

00:01:52.510 --> 00:01:54.330
said his ex-wife's
attorney would be allowed

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:57.270
to fight in her place as
her, quote "champion."

00:01:57.270 --> 00:01:59.830
Mr. Ostrom defended the
legality of this request

00:01:59.830 --> 00:02:01.217
before the court by writing quote,

00:02:01.217 --> 00:02:03.020
"Trial by combat was still regarded

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:05.280
as a legitimate method
for dispute resolution

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:07.370
when the constitution was
ratified in the United States

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:09.350
by the original 13 colonies.

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:10.850
To this day, trial by combat

00:02:10.850 --> 00:02:14.290
has never explicitly been
banned or restricted as a right

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:16.090
in these United States."

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:19.840
Check mate. Never rescinded. Still okay.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:21.733
That's how the law works, right?

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:26.950
So Mr. Ostrom also requested
a three month delay

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:29.600
so he could obtain two
samurai swords for the fight.

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:32.550
In opposition to Mr.
Ostrom's medieval motion,

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:34.140
the counsel for Ostrom's ex-wife,

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:36.567
who refers to himself in
the response as quote,

00:02:36.567 --> 00:02:39.240
"potential combatant," very cheeky,

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:42.087
that is a excellent
defining term, argued quote,

00:02:42.087 --> 00:02:44.330
"Although the respondent
and potential combatant

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:45.930
do have souls to be rended,

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:47.490
they respectfully request that the court

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:48.810
not order this done.

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:51.950
We humbly request that the
court deny this motion,

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:54.710
as the potentially life
ending ramifications

00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:56.370
surely outweigh the severity

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:58.450
of the petitioner's proposed legal remedy

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:01.100
of trying to avoid
responsibility for property taxes

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:04.370
and to acquire additional
telephonic communication.

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:07.910
What a buzzkill, seriously.

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:09.880
Now I regret to inform you that the judge

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:11.990
denied Mr. Ostrom's motion,

00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:13.960
while granting opposing counsel's request

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:17.280
to temporarily suspend Mr.
Ostrom's child visitation rights

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:20.240
and order a psychological evaluation.

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:24.150
Like a guy can't just request
trial by combat to the death?

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:26.680
I mean, judges.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:28.520
Mr. Ostrom was declared sane

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:31.120
and then demanded his
ex-wife and her attorney

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:33.010
also get sanity tests.

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:35.850
Mr. Ostrom insisted he was
neither violent, nor crazy,

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:37.700
and had no intention of hurting anyone.

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:39.460
Rather, he was simply frustrated

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:40.930
with what he believed was a system

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:43.320
stacked against men in custody disputes

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:44.560
with financial support

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:47.430
and wanted to draw attention to the issue.

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:48.710
Now trial by combat

00:03:48.710 --> 00:03:52.560
is technically illegal
in almost every state.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:54.640
And in fact, in Kentucky of all places,

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:56.680
there is an anti trial by combat law

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:58.060
that says every elected official

00:03:58.060 --> 00:04:01.530
who takes the oath of office
must actually swear before God

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:04.180
that they never fought in
a dual with deadly weapons

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:07.280
nor challenged or aided any in such fight.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:09.480
Now #notlegaladvice,

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:12.530
regardless of the legality
of trial by combat,

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:13.760
it's probably a bad idea

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:15.490
to settle disputes with deadly weapons,

00:04:15.490 --> 00:04:17.420
especially if you wanna
get elected in Kentucky.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:20.050
- Nor have I sent nor accepted a challenge

00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:22.640
to fight a dual with deadly weapons.

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:23.930
- [Devin] But that takes us to perhaps

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:26.460
the most bitter divorce
filing of all time.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:27.660
And as you just saw,

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:29.610
emotions can run high
in matters of the heart.

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:31.010
That's why for divorces,

00:04:31.010 --> 00:04:32.930
it's often a good idea to hire an attorney

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:35.700
to proceed with an air of professionalism.

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:37.500
Or you could just choose the path

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.740
of Texas attorney Paul Frank Hensler,

00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:42.930
who handled his own divorce
with a handwritten petition

00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:45.110
that was um...

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:45.970
Well, it was interesting.

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:47.660
Let's just take a look at this.

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:48.493
Now fair warning,

00:04:48.493 --> 00:04:52.300
this is a 1985 divorce
petition from Texas,

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:54.900
so don't be surprised from what follows,

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:57.540
where it's not exactly the
most evolved of pleadings.

00:04:57.540 --> 00:04:59.900
And in what reads like a
badly written country song,

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:02.780
or honestly an awesome country song,

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:04.460
Hensler states his wife
moved outta the house

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:07.790
after only 10 months of holy matrimony

00:05:07.790 --> 00:05:11.400
after she got pissed off and hauled ass

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:15.540
with their car, the
MasterCard, her $365 in cash,

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:17.420
her federal civil rights

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:20.610
nine year old employment
discrimination case

00:05:20.610 --> 00:05:22.820
against the Texas Department
of Human Resources

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:25.000
to which she is welcome,

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:27.920
having board me stiff for two years

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:30.663
about just how everybody picks on her.

00:05:32.090 --> 00:05:33.470
So Hensler declares that

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:35.780
the marriage has become very unsupportable

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:38.820
due to a conflict of personalities
between he and his wife,

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:41.240
but says the real blame
lies with his ex-wife's

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:42.557
failure to provide the quote

00:05:42.557 --> 00:05:44.960
"legitimate ends of the marriage

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:47.740
that prevents any reasonable
expectation of reconciliation,

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:51.530
unless she consents to having
her mouth surgically closed."

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:53.070
My God, man.

00:05:53.070 --> 00:05:56.350
Holy cow, you put this
in front of the court.

00:05:56.350 --> 00:05:58.650
Now Hensler attests that he and his wife

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:00.457
had no children together, although quote,

00:06:00.457 --> 00:06:02.220
"Petitioner swears on oath

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:04.567
he did everything he
could to knock her up."

00:06:07.751 --> 00:06:10.380
That's not even germaine
to the pleading here.

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:13.517
But Hensler sarcastically
says his wife is quote,

00:06:13.517 --> 00:06:17.410
"Liberated now and feminists
don't have children

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:21.890
by male chauvinist pig
lawyers, so she swears."

00:06:21.890 --> 00:06:25.850
Gosh, I can't believe this
marriage only lasted 10 months.

00:06:25.850 --> 00:06:28.170
Now Hensler requests the
court divide their estate

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:30.200
among parties based on possession,

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:32.770
clarifying he means the
legal sense of possession,

00:06:32.770 --> 00:06:34.969
not possession like in horror movies.

00:06:34.969 --> 00:06:38.630
But Hensler does assert his
wife could easily stand in

00:06:38.630 --> 00:06:41.720
for quote, "The girl from the Exorcist."

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:43.820
- I'm the holy spirit.
(girl growls)

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:45.910
- Hensler requests the
court grant his divorce

00:06:45.910 --> 00:06:48.140
and have his wife's name legally changed

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:51.660
to the demonic Bella Abzug, Jr.,

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:53.270
a play on the name Beelzebub.

00:06:53.270 --> 00:06:55.467
Hensler then closes the
petition with quote,

00:06:55.467 --> 00:06:57.140
"Screw you (beep),"

00:06:57.140 --> 00:06:59.007
while signing the pleading with

00:06:59.007 --> 00:07:01.730
"Respectfully submitted, Paul F. Hensler".

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:04.170
Fun fact, lawyers who sign
things "respectfully,"

00:07:04.170 --> 00:07:05.080
nine times outta 10

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:07.760
were secretly meaning no respect intended.

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.010
Except me, of course.

00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:12.137
Always with due respect.

00:07:12.137 --> 00:07:12.970
#notalllawyers.

00:07:13.847 --> 00:07:15.250
But that brings us to the defense attorney

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:18.760
who demanded that everyone
call him Captain Justice.

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:21.300
Now to promote the fair
administration of justice,

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:23.410
courts serve as evidentiary gatekeepers

00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:25.930
to ensure only reliable
and authenticated evidence

00:07:25.930 --> 00:07:27.170
is admitted at trial,

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:29.560
while excluding any evidence
that needlessly inflames,

00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:32.420
confuses, or prejudices the trier of fact.

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:34.910
But in one Tennessee burglary case,

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:37.220
the dueling efforts of
prosecutors and defense counsel

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:40.010
to obtain a fair trial took a very bizarre

00:07:40.010 --> 00:07:41.530
and let's call it a humorous turn.

00:07:41.530 --> 00:07:43.910
Now, back in 2013, the state of Tennessee

00:07:43.910 --> 00:07:46.060
was scheduled to prosecute Donald Powell

00:07:46.060 --> 00:07:47.560
for aggravated burglary.

00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:50.060
Assistant District Attorney
General Tammy Rettig

00:07:50.060 --> 00:07:52.440
was the local prosecutor
who represented the state,

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:54.060
while Powell was represented by

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:56.540
inappropriately named Drew Justice.

00:07:56.540 --> 00:07:59.270
Before trial, ADA Rettig
filed a motion in limine

00:07:59.270 --> 00:08:00.660
to get the court to exclude evidence

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:03.220
she believed would unfairly
prejudice the state's case.

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:05.580
Her request stopped defense counsel

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:07.900
from referring to the
state's legal representative

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:11.490
as "the Government", because
that's not very nice.

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:12.323
Yes, that's right.

00:08:12.323 --> 00:08:15.652
The prosecutor, who represented
the government of Tennessee,

00:08:15.652 --> 00:08:17.630
demanded that the defense
counsel be prohibited

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:19.500
from calling her "the Government"

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:23.280
because it might bias the jury
against, let me see here...

00:08:28.590 --> 00:08:30.210
The government.
(book slams)

00:08:30.210 --> 00:08:32.470
Now in ADA Rettig's one page motion,

00:08:32.470 --> 00:08:34.970
she suggested Mr. Justice's
repeated references

00:08:34.970 --> 00:08:36.760
to the state's attorney
as "the Government"

00:08:36.760 --> 00:08:38.820
was derogatory and prejudicial
to the state's case

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:40.450
and Mr. Justice should instead refer

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:43.360
to the state's attorneys
by their names or titles.

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:45.680
Mr. Justice responded
to this baffling motion

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:47.827
with his own appropriately
cheeky response.

00:08:47.827 --> 00:08:50.370
"The government has moved to
ban the word government.,"

00:08:50.370 --> 00:08:51.410
Mr. Justice begins,

00:08:51.410 --> 00:08:53.157
noting that the state of Tennessee quote,

00:08:53.157 --> 00:08:55.320
"Offers precisely zero legal authority

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:57.180
for this rather nitpicky position."

00:08:57.180 --> 00:08:59.150
Mr. Justice argues granting such a motion

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:01.140
would violate his first amendment rights.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:03.400
Mr. Justice asserts that
the term "the Government"

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:04.820
is not inherently derogatory,

00:09:04.820 --> 00:09:06.960
particularly since courts frequently refer

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:09.430
to the prosecutor's office
as "the Government."

00:09:09.430 --> 00:09:11.410
In the alternative, Mr. Justice argues

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:14.660
that if the ADA gets
to choose her own name,

00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:15.820
then we the defense should

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:18.130
get to choose our own names as well.

00:09:18.130 --> 00:09:19.650
Mr. Justice first requested the court

00:09:19.650 --> 00:09:21.750
stop referring to the
defendant as defendant,

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:24.087
stating that the word has a
negative connotation that quote,

00:09:24.087 --> 00:09:26.520
"Dehumanizes Mr. Donald Powell."

00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:28.820
Mr. Justice instead proposed
calling his defendant

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:31.467
by his full name, Mr.
Donald Powell, quote,

00:09:31.467 --> 00:09:34.790
"The citizen accused"
or "That innocent man."

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:36.520
But Mr. Justice was not yet finished.

00:09:36.520 --> 00:09:39.060
He asked the court that he
no longer be referred to

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:42.240
by the meager name of lawyer or attorney.

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:44.630
That's when Drew Justice
went full Ted Mosby.

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:46.180
- Pleased to meet you captain.

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:49.020
I'm Galactic President
Superstar McAwesomeville.

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:50.780
- [Devin] First, Mr. Justice
suggested that the court

00:09:50.780 --> 00:09:53.550
call him "Defender of the Innocent,"

00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:56.630
as all defendants are presumed
innocent until proven guilty.

00:09:56.630 --> 00:09:59.790
He then proposed the title
of "Guardian of the Realm."

00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:03.467
Mr. Justice also suggested if
ADA Rettig gets to be quote,

00:10:03.467 --> 00:10:05.230
"Assistant District Attorney General,"

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:06.810
then defense counsel
deserves an appropriate

00:10:06.810 --> 00:10:10.360
military title to match,
"Captain Justice."

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:13.810
Mr. Justice, sorry,
Captain Justice argued that

00:10:13.810 --> 00:10:16.240
the court shouldn't even
be calling him the defense,

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:19.630
writing the quote, "whole
idea of being defensive

00:10:19.630 --> 00:10:22.380
comes across to most
people as suspicious."

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:24.270
The captain then proposed that his side

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:26.470
instead be dubbed "The resistance."

00:10:26.470 --> 00:10:27.950
And as a "Star Wars" fan,

00:10:27.950 --> 00:10:30.080
I can certainly see the
appeal of that last one.

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:32.470
But the cheeky defense
counsel closed his motion

00:10:32.470 --> 00:10:34.577
with a similarly rye fashion, quote,

00:10:34.577 --> 00:10:37.100
"Wherefore Captain Justice,
Guardian of the Realm,

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:38.560
and Leader of the Resistance,

00:10:38.560 --> 00:10:40.780
primarily asks that the
court deny the state's motion

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:42.230
as lacking legal basis.

00:10:42.230 --> 00:10:44.130
Alternatively, the Citizen Accused

00:10:44.130 --> 00:10:45.360
moves for an order in limine

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:47.750
modifying the speech
code as aforementioned,

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:50.940
and requiring all other
euphemisms and feel-good terms

00:10:50.940 --> 00:10:53.400
as the court finds appropriate."

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:56.580
Now you might have thought
that lawyers are incapable

00:10:56.580 --> 00:10:59.750
of committing extensive trolling in court,

00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:03.380
but this motion shows
just how wrong you are.

00:11:03.380 --> 00:11:06.330
Yeah, sometimes when the
prosecution does ridiculous things,

00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:09.500
you gotta just troll the crap out of him.

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:11.120
Now sadly, the court denied

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:13.360
the Assistant District
Attorney General's motion,

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:15.230
while also denying
defense counsel's request

00:11:15.230 --> 00:11:16.940
to be called Captain Justice.

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:19.320
Tennessee's fears that being
called "the Government"

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:22.090
would prejudice their case
turned out to be unfounded.

00:11:22.090 --> 00:11:23.640
After waiving his right to a jury trial,

00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:25.560
Mr. Powell was, in fact,

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:27.800
convicted of attempted aggravated burglary

00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:30.060
and his conviction was upheld on appeal.

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:31.940
But it seems like Mr. Justice's suggestion

00:11:31.940 --> 00:11:35.290
that his client be called
quote, "That Innocent Man"

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:37.710
was just a little bit premature,

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:40.000
if not incredibly petty trolling.

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:41.850
So A+ on that.

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:43.970
But that takes us to an
actual meritorious motion

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:46.880
because one of the best
reasons, if not the best reason,

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:48.750
to ask for a continuance

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:51.310
is that the Chiefs made
it to the Super Bowl, man.

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:53.230
Now of the many skills
that lawyers possess,

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:55.550
one we certainly lack is the
ability to see the future.

00:11:55.550 --> 00:11:57.920
But one possible exception is DUI attorney

00:11:57.920 --> 00:12:00.300
and Kansas City Chiefs
super fan Denise Kirby,

00:12:00.300 --> 00:12:02.430
who successfully predicted
in a legal filing

00:12:02.430 --> 00:12:05.180
that the Chiefs would break a
50 year championship drought

00:12:05.180 --> 00:12:06.420
that would render her too busy

00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:10.150
cheering on her team at Super
Bowl 54 to attend trial.

00:12:10.150 --> 00:12:11.460
Here's how it went down.

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:13.940
Now in October 2019,
Ms. Kirby filed a motion

00:12:13.940 --> 00:12:16.940
to continue her February
3rd, 2020 DUI trial

00:12:16.940 --> 00:12:18.740
on the grounds that she'd
personally be in Miami

00:12:18.740 --> 00:12:21.410
watching her team play in Super Bowl 54.

00:12:21.410 --> 00:12:23.930
At the time of the motion,
the concept was laughable.

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:26.060
So much so, that apparently
everyone in the courtroom

00:12:26.060 --> 00:12:27.740
laughed at her request.

00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:29.870
But then the Chiefs made
it to the Super Bowl.

00:12:29.870 --> 00:12:32.510
So Ms. Kirby filed a new
motion to continue trial.

00:12:32.510 --> 00:12:34.297
According to Ms. Kirby's motion, quote,

00:12:34.297 --> 00:12:35.720
"The courtroom erupted in laughter"

00:12:35.720 --> 00:12:38.010
when she confidently asserted in October

00:12:38.010 --> 00:12:39.130
that she would be in Miami

00:12:39.130 --> 00:12:41.110
to watch the Chiefs in the Super Bowl."

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:42.900
She further noted that
the court had advised

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:46.120
that should that happen, it
would grant the continuance.

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:48.900
Quote, "It happened," wrote Ms. Kirby.

00:12:48.900 --> 00:12:51.720
As a result, Ms. Kirby would
not be back in time for trial

00:12:51.720 --> 00:12:53.360
and thus needed a continuance.

00:12:53.360 --> 00:12:56.110
The motion ends with quote, "Go Chiefs!"

00:12:56.110 --> 00:12:57.940
Because of course it does.

00:12:57.940 --> 00:12:59.750
Now ultimately the Chiefs and Ms. Kirby

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:01.270
would have the last laugh.

00:13:01.270 --> 00:13:03.120
In a historic fourth quarter comeback,

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:05.050
the Chiefs overcame a 10 point deficit

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:06.860
with 21 unanswered points

00:13:06.860 --> 00:13:09.400
to beat the San Francisco 49ers 31 to 20.

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:11.623
It was heartbreaking.

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:13.980
I was born in San Francisco.

00:13:13.980 --> 00:13:15.283
I'm a big 49ers fan.

00:13:16.990 --> 00:13:17.823
Sorry.

00:13:17.823 --> 00:13:20.490
The court, having granted
Ms. Kirby's continuance,

00:13:20.490 --> 00:13:21.520
helped fulfill the prophecy

00:13:21.520 --> 00:13:24.440
that allowed her to see
that historic victory.

00:13:24.440 --> 00:13:27.980
And that takes us to the
importance of being earnest.

00:13:27.980 --> 00:13:28.813
Hemingway.

00:13:28.813 --> 00:13:31.440
Now lawyers have a reputation
for being humorless,

00:13:31.440 --> 00:13:32.400
buttoned-up suits.

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:33.680
- Well, I'm a professional.

00:13:33.680 --> 00:13:36.130
I'm serious and I'm a professional.

00:13:36.130 --> 00:13:37.660
- Can't imagine why.

00:13:37.660 --> 00:13:41.010
But we lawyer-types love to
cut loose and have some fun.

00:13:41.010 --> 00:13:42.530
So what is an attorney to do

00:13:42.530 --> 00:13:45.660
when our extracurricular
activities clash with trial dates?

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:48.510
Well, if you are Florida
lawyer, Frank Louderback,

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:49.760
getting ready to attend

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:51.660
an Ernest Hemingway Look-Alike Contest,

00:13:51.660 --> 00:13:53.670
you hope that your court is understanding

00:13:53.670 --> 00:13:55.220
of your scheduling conflict

00:13:55.220 --> 00:13:58.840
and non-refundable deposits, as well.

00:13:58.840 --> 00:14:00.060
The court was not.

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:01.110
Here's what happened.

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:03.770
In 2012, Florida man Jerry Allen Bottorff

00:14:03.770 --> 00:14:05.430
was facing federal charges

00:14:05.430 --> 00:14:07.260
in connection with a murder-for-hire plot

00:14:07.260 --> 00:14:09.230
involving the murder victim's wife,

00:14:09.230 --> 00:14:11.040
Cristie Sehorne-Bottorff,

00:14:11.040 --> 00:14:13.200
whom Jerry had met at a swinger's club,

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:14.830
and who later became Jerry's wife.

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:17.360
Just your typical Florida love story.

00:14:17.360 --> 00:14:19.390
Now, Frank Louderback was scheduled

00:14:19.390 --> 00:14:21.230
to go to trial in July of 2012,

00:14:21.230 --> 00:14:23.910
but everything changed for
the St. Petersburg lawyer

00:14:23.910 --> 00:14:25.530
when he became a semi-finalist

00:14:25.530 --> 00:14:28.700
in the annual Ernest Hemingway
Look-Alike Competition

00:14:28.700 --> 00:14:31.940
at Sloppy Joe's Bar in Key West.

00:14:31.940 --> 00:14:34.210
Now Louderback understandably felt

00:14:34.210 --> 00:14:36.260
that this fortuitous
change in circumstances

00:14:36.260 --> 00:14:38.070
merited a brief suspension of trial,

00:14:38.070 --> 00:14:39.357
informing the court quote,

00:14:39.357 --> 00:14:42.210
"Undersigned counsel has
secured a block of six rooms

00:14:42.210 --> 00:14:44.830
to accommodate family, friends and fans

00:14:44.830 --> 00:14:47.650
and has had to pay
non-refundable deposits."

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:49.660
Now non-refundable
deposits not withstanding,

00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:52.300
US District Court Judge Steven D. Merryday

00:14:52.300 --> 00:14:53.937
denied the request writing quote,

00:14:53.937 --> 00:14:55.840
"Between a murder-for-hire trial

00:14:55.840 --> 00:14:57.670
and an annual look-alike contest,

00:14:57.670 --> 00:15:00.460
surely Hemingway, a perfervid admirer

00:15:00.460 --> 00:15:04.520
of quote 'grace under pressure'
would choose the trial."

00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:05.740
And in his denial,

00:15:05.740 --> 00:15:07.800
Judge Merryday showcased
his own sense of humor

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:09.020
and admiration for Hemingway,

00:15:09.020 --> 00:15:11.580
citing Dorothy Parker's
1929 New Yorker profile

00:15:11.580 --> 00:15:12.427
of the author, quote,

00:15:12.427 --> 00:15:13.420
"At his most robust,

00:15:13.420 --> 00:15:15.520
Hemingway exemplified the
intrepid defense lawyer.

00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:16.940
He works like hell and through it.

00:15:16.940 --> 00:15:18.730
He has the most profound bravery.

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:21.160
He has had pain and the kind of poverty

00:15:21.160 --> 00:15:22.040
that you don't believe.

00:15:22.040 --> 00:15:23.820
He has had about eight times

00:15:23.820 --> 00:15:25.960
the normal allotment of responsibilities.

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:27.590
And he has never once compromised.

00:15:27.590 --> 00:15:29.820
He has never turned off on an easier path

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:31.190
than the one he staked himself.

00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:32.910
It takes courage."

00:15:32.910 --> 00:15:34.250
Judge Merryday closes the motion

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:36.100
by citing the iconic final line

00:15:36.100 --> 00:15:37.920
of Hemingway's "The Sun Also Rises."

00:15:37.920 --> 00:15:38.830
And you've gotta love the way

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:40.270
that the judge ends this order.

00:15:40.270 --> 00:15:42.300
Best of luck to counsel
in next year's contest.

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:44.790
The motion docket 127 is denied.

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:47.590
And while Louderback would
live to compete another day,

00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:50.290
sadly Bottorff and his wife
pleaded guilty to the charges

00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:51.540
and were sentenced to life in prison

00:15:51.540 --> 00:15:54.660
and in perhaps the greatest
miscarriage of justice,

00:15:54.660 --> 00:15:58.930
would never live to see a
Hemingway look-alike contest.

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:01.330
